, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical: same status codes, same response bodies. Need full refactored file. Need likely define sentinel errors: errInvalidID, errUserNotFound, errDatabase? But external behavior: 400 body {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no Content-Type? Original for 400/404/500 does not set Content-Type. For success sets Content-Type application/json and encodes map. JSON encoder adds newline. Need preserve exact response bodies? It says same response bodies. For success, json.Encoder.Encode writes {\"email\":...,\"name\":...} + \"\\n\" because map keys sorted alphabetically: email then name. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal and w.Write, body would lack newline, not identical. So use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode for success. For errors, write exact bytes no newline. Need ensure no Content-Type on errors. If we create helper writeJSONError", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0030493689700961113], [760, -6.889895915985107]], [[1144, -1.2755474926962052e-05], [14235, -12.074366569519043]], [[4087, -0.013568666763603687], [310, -4.484502792358398]], [[1156, -0.04033331573009491], [303, -3.381929874420166]], [[579, -0.21730557084083557], [25, -2.3488974571228027]], [[1622, -0.003175227902829647], [3296, -6.4940619468688965]], [[13, -0.3490358293056488], [25, -1.6215521097183228]], [[14235, -0.031883761286735535], [1165, -4.235035419464111]], [[89109, -0.32547780871391296], [7936, -1.8338738679885864]], [[5805, -0.00023636034165974706], [2400, -8.755271911621094]], [[9830, -0.02406155690550804], [6795, -3.793640613555908]], [[6795, -2.8729851692332886e-05], [17369, -11.912979125976562]], [[1083, -1.4096304178237915], [47781, -1.5933042764663696]], [[1228, -0.10285717248916626], [2400, -2.72688627243042]], [[470, -3.278309304732829e-05], [5568, -10.62187385559082]], [[5568, -0.0028367305640131235], [74243, -6.207216739654541]], [[440, -0.9293662309646606], [25, -1.900015950202942]], [[2708, -0.0388290